The format marks the file manager draws on a file's page come from devicon too,
under the same MIT License: apache.svg, bash.svg, cmake.svg, cplusplus.svg,
csharp.svg, css3.svg, dart.svg, elixir.svg, haskell.svg, html5.svg, java.svg,
javascript.svg, json.svg, kotlin.svg, latex.svg, lua.svg, markdown.svg,
perl.svg, php.svg, pnpm.svg, powershell.svg, r.svg, react.svg, ruby.svg,
rust.svg, sass.svg, scala.svg, svelte.svg, swift.svg, tailwindcss.svg,
typescript.svg, vitejs.svg, vuejs.svg, xml.svg, yaml.svg, yarn.svg and zig.svg
are its <name>-original.svg and graphql.svg its graphql-plain.svg, unchanged;
c.svg is c-original.svg as of devicon v2.15.1, whose hexagon reads on a page
where the later letterform's pale grey does not.

pnpm-light.svg is devicon's pnpm-original.svg, as pnpm.svg is, with its
charcoal #4c4c4c lifted to #a4a4a4, the same grey at the L 0.72 rung, for the
tile a package manager is drawn on; pnpm.svg stays as it was for the file
manager's paper page.

mono/ holds the single-colour marks pressed into a folder's face. Every file
there is from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org), CC0 1.0, unchanged, renamed
after the product key the folders use: nodedotjs.svg is nodejs.svg,
nextdotjs.svg nextjs.svg, letsencrypt.svg lets-encrypt.svg, rubygems.svg
ruby.svg, openjdk.svg java.svg, visualstudiocode.svg vscode.svg and gnubash.svg
bash.svg.
